WEBVTT

00:09:57.005 --> 00:10:00.530
Let's assume Singapore comes up

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.584
with a Cap And Trade scheme

00:10:02.584 --> 00:10:04.339
for the power sector.

00:10:04.339 --> 00:10:07.820
That means all electricity-generating

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.830
and related companies would

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.764
be part of this scheme.

00:10:11.764 --> 00:10:14.060
The government announces that

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.589
they are putting a cap of

00:10:15.589 --> 00:10:16.880
10,000 tonnes of

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:20.285
CO2 emissions on the power interest rate,

00:10:20.285 --> 00:10:23.029
which means all companies

00:10:23.029 --> 00:10:24.920
combined are allowed to

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:29.345
emit only 10,000 tonnes of CO2 in a year.

00:10:29.345 --> 00:10:32.480
For simplicity, let's assume that

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.040
there are only two companies

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:35.434
in our power sector,

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:37.970
Company A and Company B.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:40.355
These 10,000 tonnes of CO2

00:10:40.355 --> 00:10:43.145
gets divided between these two.

00:10:43.145 --> 00:10:45.140
Now, they both have

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:48.524
a cap of 5,000 tonnes of CO2.

00:10:48.524 --> 00:10:50.784
When the year ends,

00:10:50.784 --> 00:10:53.170
this is their emission portfolio.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.300
Company A emitted

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.895
only 3,000 tonnes of CO2,

00:10:57.895 --> 00:11:00.399
which means Company A

00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:04.239
reduced much more than they were required to.

00:11:04.239 --> 00:11:07.930
Now, they have unused permits,

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:11.259
worth 2,000 tonnes of CO2.

00:11:11.259 --> 00:11:13.120
On the other hand,

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:17.335
Company B emitted 7,000 tonnes of CO2.

00:11:17.335 --> 00:11:19.480
That means they have

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:22.824
exceeded the limit by 2,000 tonnes,

00:11:22.824 --> 00:11:25.915
and they must do something about it,

00:11:25.915 --> 00:11:28.464
as the government instructed them

00:11:28.464 --> 00:11:31.320
to emit only 5,000 tonnes.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:34.550
What Cap And Trade does is it allows

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:38.030
Company A and Company B to trade

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:40.609
their permits in a market.

00:11:40.609 --> 00:11:43.865
Company A has unused permits,

00:11:43.865 --> 00:11:46.895
amounting to 2,000 tonnes of CO2,

00:11:46.895 --> 00:11:48.830
and Company B has

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:51.830
a shortfall of emission permits.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.960
What they do is they

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.134
go into the market and Company A

00:11:56.134 --> 00:11:58.399
sells the 2,000 tonnes'

00:11:58.399 --> 00:12:01.100
worth of permits to Company B.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:04.144
Company B buys it and now

00:12:04.144 --> 00:12:08.209
they can easily meet their emission mandate.

00:12:08.209 --> 00:12:11.719
The question we should ask is why

00:12:11.719 --> 00:12:14.419
Company B was allowed to

00:12:14.419 --> 00:12:17.765
emit more than their permissible permits,

00:12:17.765 --> 00:12:20.549
and how they got away with it.

00:12:20.549 --> 00:12:22.159
They did not.

00:12:22.159 --> 00:12:24.019
They got punished.

00:12:24.019 --> 00:12:26.059
They were forced to go to

00:12:26.059 --> 00:12:27.920
the emission trading market and

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:30.214
buy additional emission permits

00:12:30.214 --> 00:12:32.120
by paying for them.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.994
On the other hand,

00:12:33.994 --> 00:12:36.799
Company A was allowed to sell

00:12:36.799 --> 00:12:38.659
their unused permits in

00:12:38.659 --> 00:12:40.595
the market at a price.

00:12:40.595 --> 00:12:43.325
In this way, they were

00:12:43.325 --> 00:12:45.259
rewarded for reducing much

00:12:45.259 --> 00:12:47.644
more than they were required to.

00:12:47.644 --> 00:12:50.240
The polluter was punished.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.290
The one who reduce its emission was rewarded.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.409
Power industry emitted only 10,000 tonnes

00:12:57.409 --> 00:13:00.259
of CO2, meeting their cap.

00:13:00.259 --> 00:13:02.299
And we were able to do so

00:13:02.299 --> 00:13:04.879
at the lowest cost possible.

00:13:04.879 --> 00:13:07.760
Win, win, win, win.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.194
Reducing emissions has a cost.

00:13:11.194 --> 00:13:13.460
But this cost may be different for

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.800
each company, based on

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.109
their size, nature of their operations

00:13:18.109 --> 00:13:20.254
and so many other factors.

00:13:20.254 --> 00:13:23.569
Reducing emissions might be cheaper for

00:13:23.569 --> 00:13:27.230
Company A in comparison to Company B.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:30.139
Rather than forcing Company B to

00:13:30.139 --> 00:13:33.125
reduce emissions at a much higher cost,

00:13:33.125 --> 00:13:37.009
Cap And Trade allows Company A to reduce more

00:13:37.009 --> 00:13:40.594
and let Company B buy from Company A.

00:13:40.594 --> 00:13:43.679
That's the beauty of Cap And Trade.

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:50.525
Now that we know how Cap And Trade works,

00:13:50.525 --> 00:13:54.510
we have answers for all of these questions.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.869
Another economic incentive-based tool

00:13:59.869 --> 00:14:01.714
is the carbon tax.

00:14:01.714 --> 00:14:04.460
It might sound familiar to you as

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.929
Singapore has recently

00:14:05.929 --> 00:14:08.719
introduced the carbon tax.

00:14:08.719 --> 00:14:10.909
Any industrial facility in

00:14:10.909 --> 00:14:13.040
Singapore that emits

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.039
25 kilotonnes of CO2 or

00:14:16.039 --> 00:14:19.715
more in a year must pay carbon tax,

00:14:19.715 --> 00:14:22.039
which is set at $5

00:14:22.039 --> 00:14:25.235
per tonne for a certain period.

00:14:25.235 --> 00:14:28.954
Talking about how it works -

00:14:28.954 --> 00:14:32.224
again, a simple schematic

00:14:32.224 --> 00:14:35.779
with seven steps can help us understand this.

00:14:35.779 --> 00:14:37.625
The very first step,

00:14:37.625 --> 00:14:40.459
the government puts a price on carbon.

00:14:40.459 --> 00:14:44.120
In Singapore, it's $5 per tonne.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.790
For every tonne of carbon,

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.444
you will pay $5.

00:14:49.444 --> 00:14:52.954
Businesses now have two options.

00:14:52.954 --> 00:14:54.860
They either pay or they

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:57.019
can try to reduce emissions.

00:14:57.019 --> 00:15:00.635
But even if they wanted to reduce emissions,




